Track 3: Ijsbreker Hakken
- Story & Context: The legendary culmination of the genre took place in an abandoned flood-control cistern beneath the Maas River during the torrential spring thaw of 1991. When an emergency relief gate broke open and sent knee-deep icy water surging across the dancefloor, the crowd of three hundred shaved-headed ravers did not disperse; they dug their heels in and stomped harder. Sweat evaporated from steaming scalps into the near-freezing vault air, mixing with the sharp scent of damp limestone dust falling like snow from the vibrating ceiling. As Valk redlined the kick drum to lock directly with the hydraulic roar of the draining river, the sodden crowd screamed in unison over the distortion: "we dance until the floor turns into river."
